# Component boundaries

## Data flow

```
app/<route>/page.tsx
  → lib/load-*.ts          (fetch)
  → lib/build-*-view-model.ts (pure assemble)
  → components/<domain>/*  (render props)
```

Pages compose. They do not contain forecast math, flag rules, or large JSX modules.

## Folders

| Folder | Owns | Must not |
|--------|------|----------|
| `app/**/page.tsx` | Route, metadata, loaders, composition | Domain markup, token invention |
| `app/**/actions.ts` | Server mutations | UI |
| `components/layout` | Shell, sidebar, wordmark, breadcrumbs, `SectionHeader` | Domain data |
| `components/ui` | Primitives (`StatusPill`) | Feature logic |
| `components/brand` | Platform logos | App chrome |
| `components/charts` | Shared chart fragments | Page layout |
| `components/release` | `/release/[id]` cockpit | Dashboard/archive tables |
| `components/dashboard` | `/` active list | Release cockpit modules |
| `components/new` | `/new` form | Release-page layout |
| `components/archive` | `/archive` | Live monitoring |
| `components/report` | Public `/report/[slug]` | Internal sidebar assumptions |
| `components/admin/retrain` | Retrain/approve | Release cockpit |
| `lib/**` | Math, flags, view models, loaders, supabase | **Any JSX** |

`lib/` never imports `components/`. Components never call `predictStreams` / `computeFlags` — they receive view-model slices.

## Cross-domain

Do not import across feature folders except:

- `components/release/ChannelMixForecast` → `components/new/AdSpendLiveForecast` (one ad-metric card)
- Any feature → `layout`, `ui`, `brand`, `charts`, `lib` types/formatters

New cockpit UI goes in `components/release/`, not `page.tsx`. New primitives go in `components/ui/`, not a feature folder.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — math in a component
const streams = predictStreams(inputs, coeffs);

// ❌ BAD — JSX in lib
export function FlagRow() { return <li>{title}</li>; }

// ✅ GOOD
const viewModel = buildReleaseViewModel(release, daily, ...);
<FlagsPanel phase={viewModel.phase} flags={viewModel.flags} />
```
